# Dev Notes 56 — Runtime Action Event History Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-20  
**Branch:** `runtime-action-event-storage-v1`  
**Status:** Repo-inspected on `runtime-action-event-storage-v1` for the declared bounded in-memory action-event history/readback scope. Assistant syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted action-event history smoke, action-event subscription regression smoke, runtime public-entrypoint guard, execute-action/cancel-action/public-dispatch/nativeWorkerBackend mock regression smokes, current contract-chain smokes, worker static/mock smokes, candidate package extraction/recheck, artifact guard, Michael local Windows/MINGW64 real-runtime execute-action/cancel-action/nativeWorkerBackend checks, and direct GitHub branch inspection passed. This corrected document updates the branch identity from the staging package name to the actual uploaded GitHub branch name.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds the first narrow history/readback seam for execute-action events.

It preserves the previous live event-subscription surface while adding:

```js
readActionEvents(filter = {}, options = {})
```

The new surface is intentionally bounded in-memory history/readback only. It does not add durable persistence, callback replay, cross-process pub/sub, stream-delta materialization, `eventLogStoreBackend`, graph runtime behavior, scheduler/request/lifecycle changes, worker changes, or native backend execution changes.

