## 3. Modular ownership

The event surfaces now remain split by responsibility:

```text
runtime/bus/actionEvent.mjs
  validation and normalization only

runtime/bus/actionEventSubscriptionRegistry.mjs
  live same-process listener registration, filtering, unsubscribe, and publication only

runtime/bus/actionEventHistory.mjs
  bounded in-memory history, retention, sequence assignment, and read/query only

runtime.mjs
  composition root; wires record -> live publish and exposes readActionEvents(...)
```

No broad event manager was introduced.

`actionEventHistory.mjs` does not import the subscription registry, `runtime.mjs`, worker bridge, worker modules, request modules, stream modules, lifecycle modules, or backend/native execution modules.

---

## 4. Public behavior

`runtime.mjs` now exports:

```text
cancelAction
cancelPrompt
executeAction
initModel
prompt
readActionEvents
resetModel
resetSession
shutdownRuntime
subscribeActionEvents
```

`readActionEvents(filter, options)` returns:

```js
{
    events: [],
    cursor: {
        lastSequence: null
    },
    truncated: false
}
```

Supported history filters:

```text
actionId
runId
type
capability
sinceTimestamp
untilTimestamp
afterSequence
```

Supported read options:

```text
limit
```

History behavior:

```text
bounded total in-memory retention, default maxEvents: 1000
record before live publication
monotonic sequence assigned at record time
events returned in sequence order
defensive frozen copies returned from reads
duplicate retained eventId values rejected
older evicted eventIds may be reused after leaving the retained window
```

---

