## 10. Caveats / known risks

### Finding: History is not durable storage

Affected surface:

```text
README/docs/API wording, future graph expectations, event replay expectations
```

Why it matters:

```text
A bounded in-memory event history disappears on process exit and is not a durable event log.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Docs call this history/readback only and explicitly defer eventLogStoreBackend.
```

### Finding: Stream deltas remain excluded

Affected surface:

```text
runtime/stream, prompt streaming semantics, executeAction future streaming events, real-runtime stream behavior
```

Why it matters:

```text
action.stream.delta would touch higher-volume ordering, storage pressure, and stream-shaping policy.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep stream-delta materialization in a separate future plan/spec branch.
```

### Finding: Storage failure policy is only safe for in-memory v1

Affected surface:

```text
executeAction publication path, action-event consistency
```

Why it matters:

```text
recordActionEvent currently runs before live publication. For in-memory v1, record failure indicates validation/configuration drift. A future durable backend needs an explicit failure policy.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Define durable storage failure policy in eventLogStoreBackend work, not in this branch.
```

